BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 693.77 Tm (Use a weighted qualification score only after applying hard exclusions. Reject unsupported provenance, prohibited) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 678.55 Tm (product handling, unclear buyer identity, negative stressed contribution, or repayment dependent on an unconfirmed) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 663.32 Tm (receipt. Score the survivors on committed demand, margin evidence, liquidity, counterparty authority, traceability, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 648.10 Tm (execution capacity, using the weights below. Require at least 85 points for a paid pilot, with no hard exclusion) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 632.87 Tm (overridden by a high aggregate score. Give full demand credit only to a commitment specifying quantity, price,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 617.65 Tm (acceptance, and expiry; a chat expressing interest earns less. Margin credit requires a landed-cost worksheet and the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 602.42 Tm (removal of unvested rewards from the downside case. Liquidity credit requires cash that remains available after payroll,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 587.20 Tm (operating expenses, existing card balances, and other obligations. Verify the payment recipient through an established) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 571.97 Tm (contact before sending funds after any bank-detail change. For a supplier relationship, examine title warranties and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 556.75 Tm (conflicting claims under applicable UCC Article 2 provisions rather than treating an invoice as conclusive proof. Keep) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 541.52 Tm (the source documents attached to the scored record so another operator can reproduce the decision without trusting the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 526.30 Tm (salesperson's memory.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 511.07 Tm (Build the cash calendar before negotiating a larger allocation. Record purchase authorization, statement close,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 495.85 Tm (contractual payment due date, carrier delivery, buyer inspection, expected ACH initiation, and cleared cash availability) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 480.62 Tm (as distinct events. Advertised statement float approaching 55 days depends on purchase timing and the actual card) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 465.40 Tm (agreement; it is not a standard maturity available on every order. Treat every card purchase as a short-term repayment) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 450.17 Tm (liability from day one. Suppose a $10,000 pilot expects cleared reimbursement on day 12, while its card payment is due) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 434.95 Tm (on day 15. A ten-day buyer delay moves receipt to day 22 and creates a seven-day funding gap. The operator must) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 419.72 Tm (already hold enough available cash to pay on day 15; a pending ACH entry does not satisfy that requirement.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 404.50 Tm (Illustratively, a $10,000 balance charged 24% annual interest for seven days costs approximately $46.03 before any fee,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 389.27 Tm (and a $35 fee raises that burden to $81.03. Actual agreements may impose different interest mechanics or remove a) Tj ET
